<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Privacy Policy - Kumix Stream</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/images/kumix-logo.png" type="image/png">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tabler/icons-webfont@2.30.0/tabler-icons.min.css">
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
  <script>
    tailwind.config = {
      theme: {
        fontFamily: { 'sans': ['Inter', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'] },
        extend: {
          colors: {
            'primary': '#E8102A',
            'secondary': '#C00D22',
            'dark': {
              '900': '#121212', '800': '#252525', '700': '#2D2D2D',
              '600': '#3D3D3D', '500': '#6E6E6E'
            }
          }
        }
      }
    };
  </script>
</head>
<body class="bg-dark-900 text-gray-300 font-sans min-h-screen flex flex-col">
  <header class="border-b border-dark-700">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/home" class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <img src="/images/kumix-logo.png" alt="Kumix Stream" class="w-7 h-7">
        <span class="text-white font-semibold">Kumix Stream</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-5 text-sm">
        <a href="/home" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
        <a href="/terms" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Terms</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 w-full">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-10">Last updated: 24 September 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Kumix Stream is a self-hosted streaming application. All data described below is stored on
          the server operated by the administrator of this instance — the software itself sends your
          data nowhere except the third-party services explicitly described in this policy.
          Questions about this instance (including data deletion requests) should be directed to its
          administrator at <a href="mailto:kumixlabs@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">kumixlabs@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="google-user-data">
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">2. Google / YouTube user data</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Kumix Stream integrates with Google's YouTube APIs through Google Sign-In (OAuth 2.0).
          This section explicitly describes what Google user data the app accesses, how the app uses
          it, and with whom it is shared. Access only happens after you explicitly connect a YouTube
          channel and approve the Google consent screen.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-1.5">2.1 What Google user data the app accesses</h3>
        <p class="mb-3">
          After you grant permission, the app requests the following OAuth scopes and accesses only
          the data below from the YouTube channel you connect:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 mb-4">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Channel identity</strong> — your YouTube channel ID, channel name, and channel avatar (profile picture URL).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Channel statistics</strong> — your channel's subscriber count, used only as a display reference.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">OAuth tokens</strong> — the access and refresh tokens issued by Google for the connected channel, stored encrypted at rest.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Broadcast and video metadata</strong> — titles, descriptions, thumbnails, tags, category, privacy status, scheduling details, and broadcast ads/monetization settings of the live broadcasts and videos the app creates or manages on your behalf.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Live stream ingestion data</strong> — the stream key and ingestion settings for broadcasts the app creates for you.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-500">
          OAuth scopes requested:
          <code class="text-xs bg-dark-800 border border-dark-600 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">youtube.readonly</code>,
          <code class="text-xs bg-dark-800 border border-dark-600 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">youtube.force-ssl</code>, and
          <code class="text-xs bg-dark-800 border border-dark-600 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5">youtube</code>.
          The app does not access your Google email, contacts, documents, browsing data, or any other Google account information.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-1.5">2.2 How the app uses Google user data</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 mb-4">
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">authenticate</strong> API requests to YouTube on your behalf using the stored OAuth tokens.</li>
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">create, schedule, update, and manage live broadcasts</strong> (title, description, thumbnail, privacy settings) on the channels you connect.</li>
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">create stream keys</strong> so the app can deliver your live video to YouTube's ingestion servers when a stream starts.</li>
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">show which channel is connected</strong> (name, avatar, subscriber count) inside the app's interface.</li>
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">keep the connection working</strong> by refreshing expired access tokens.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Google user data is used solely to provide these streaming features. It is not used for
          advertising, profiling, analytics, or any unrelated purpose, and it is not used to serve
          ads or to train any model.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-gray-200 font-semibold mb-1.5">2.3 With whom the app shares Google user data</h3>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-gray-200">Kumix Stream does not sell, rent, share, transfer, or disclose Google user data to any third party.</strong>
          The only disclosures that occur are:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>To <strong class="text-gray-200">Google itself</strong>, when the app calls YouTube APIs on your behalf (the data goes back to the service it came from).</li>
          <li>To the <strong class="text-gray-200">server hosting this instance</strong>, because the connected channel's data and encrypted tokens are stored in this instance's database.</li>
          <li>When <strong class="text-gray-200">required by law</strong>, to the extent legally compelled.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          There are no advertising networks, data brokers, or analytics providers involved. When you
          disconnect a YouTube channel from the app's settings, its stored tokens and channel data
          are removed. You can also revoke the app's access at any time from your Google account's
          third-party access page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">3. Other information the app handles</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Account data</strong> — username, password (stored only as a cryptographic hash), and optional profile avatar.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Uploaded media</strong> — videos, audio files, and thumbnails you upload, stored on the server's disk.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Stream configuration</strong> — stream titles, schedules, and RTMP stream keys for the platforms you stream to.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Session cookies</strong> — a single login-session cookie keeping you signed in. No tracking or advertising cookies are used.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Technical logs</strong> — application logs and per-stream FFmpeg logs kept on the server for troubleshooting.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">4. Third-party services</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Google / YouTube APIs</strong> — used strictly as described in section 2 above, with your explicit consent. You can revoke this at any time from the app's settings or your Google account's third-party access page.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Streaming destinations</strong> — when a stream starts, its video is delivered to the RTMP destination you configured (e.g. YouTube ingestion servers).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">These third parties process your data under their own privacy policies.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">5. Data retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Media, streams, history, and connected channels can be deleted at any time from within the
          app. Disconnecting a YouTube channel removes its stored tokens and channel data. The
          administrator of this instance can additionally purge any residual data from the server.
          You may also request deletion of your data by contacting
          <a href="mailto:kumixlabs@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">kumixlabs@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">6. Limited Use</h2>
        <p>
          Kumix Stream's use of Google user data complies with the
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
          including the Limited Use requirements. Google user data is only used to provide the
          publicly advertised features of the app (YouTube live stream management) and is never
          transferred to third parties for their own independent purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">7. What this app does not do</h2>
        <p>
          No analytics, no advertising, no profiling, and no selling or sharing of your data with
          anyone beyond the third-party services described above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy is updated, the new version will be published on this page with a revised
          "Last updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy question or data request regarding this instance, contact
          <a href="mailto:kumixlabs@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">kumixlabs@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-dark-700">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
      <span>&copy; 2026 Kumix Stream</span>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-5">
        <a href="/home" class="hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors">Home</a>
        <a href="/terms" class="hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors">Terms of Service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
